<!--
  World fragment loaded via Include src= (see index.html shell).
  Edit this file — do not paste into index.html.

  COORDINATE GOTCHA — `at` on <FarmPlot> is the centre of cell (0,0), not the
  centre of the grid (farm-plot/grid.ts:4-5). With cell-size 1 and size 24x18
  the tiles run from at → at + (23, 17). The old world declared at="0 10" and
  then drew a SpawnExclusion r=15.5 around (0,10), which left the far corner of
  the plot (x=23.5) outside the exclusion — vegetation spawned on the crops.

  Here the grid is centred on the farm pad at (-86, 6):
      at = (-86, 6) - (23/2, 17/2) = (-97.5, -2.5)
      tiles span x ∈ [-98, -74], z ∈ [-3, 15]
  The exclusion is centred on the real grid centre with a radius that clears
  the half-diagonal (√(12² + 9²) = 15) plus the yard.

  base-y must equal the pad height in terrain.xml (11).
-->
<Group name="farm" pos="0 0 0">
  <FarmPlot
    at="-97.5 -2.5"
    size="24 18"
    cell-size="1"
    base-y="11"
  ></FarmPlot>

  <SpawnExclusion at="-86 6" radius="30"></SpawnExclusion>

  <!-- Barn yard, north edge of the pad and clear of the tiles. -->
